Subject: The push-buffer thread's state is thread-local under every compiler

nv2a_pb_exec.c chose __declspec(thread) for any Windows target. clang and GCC targeting mingw ignore
that attribute with a warning, so its per-thread state became one variable shared by every thread. The
qualifier is now chosen by the compiler, as recomp_types.h and xbox_winnt.h already do.

---
diff --git a/src/kernel/nv2a_pb_exec.c b/src/kernel/nv2a_pb_exec.c
--- a/src/kernel/nv2a_pb_exec.c
+++ b/src/kernel/nv2a_pb_exec.c
@@ -39,6 +39,9 @@
 #include "nv2a_combiner.h"
 #if defined(_WIN32)
 #include <windows.h>
+#endif
+/* Keyed on the compiler: clang and GCC targeting Windows ignore __declspec(thread). */
+#if defined(_MSC_VER)
 #define NV_TLS __declspec(thread)
 #else
 #define NV_TLS __thread
